===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|hovet}}, {{m|dum|hooft}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|hōvit}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*haubudą}}, ultimately from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*kauput-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kaput-}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|Höft}}, German {{m|de|Haupt}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|haed}}, English {{m|en|head}}, Danish {{m|da|hoved}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɦoːft/|lang=nl}}
* {{audio|Nl-hoofd.ogg|audio|lang=nl}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|n|-en|hoofdje}}

# {{lb|nl|anatomy}} [[head]]
# [[head]] (''of an organisation''), [[chief]], [[boss]]
# a breakwater, jetty or pier at the entrance of a sea harbour
# {{lb|nl|slang}} oral sex, from the English slang sense of {{l|en|head}}

====Derived terms====
These are derived terms from the meaning "the head of a body". The prefix "[[hoofd-]]" means "main, head, chief", so words derived from that meaning are listed on ''[[hoofd-]]''.
{{top4}}
* {{l|nl|hoofdpijn}}
* {{l|nl|uit het hoofd}}
* {{l|nl|staatshoofd}}
{{mid2}}
* {{l|nl|voorhoofd}}
* {{l|nl|havenhoofd}}
{{bottom}}

